[ti:Copper on the Terrace]
[Intro]
[Verse 1]
[00:15.30] Champagne flutes on the limestone ledge
[00:19.45] Three dozen stories above the avenue hedge
[00:23.20] You’re leaning back in your linen shirt
[00:26.50] Laughing too loud so the truth won't hurt
[00:31.20] The sun drops low like a minted coin
[00:34.90] Where the rusted girders and brick adjoin
[00:38.80] Everyone’s acting like August stayed
[00:42.50] While the terrace shadows begin to trade
[Pre-Chorus]
[00:46.40] There’s a sudden bite in the evening air
[00:50.40] And you trace the rim of your crystal ware
[00:54.20] You look at the skyline, not at me
[00:57.90] Like a ship already out to sea
[Chorus]
[01:02.00] It’s copper on the terrace, gold turning to rust
[01:06.00] All of our promises ground into velvet dust
[01:10.00] Dance me to the edge of the balcony rail
[01:13.90] Before the warm trade winds begin to fail
[01:17.80] You’re holding my waist like a souvenir
[01:21.80] In the brightest hour of a dying year
[01:25.80] Yeah, it’s copper on the terrace tonight
[Verse 2]
[01:34.10] Your best friend’s spinning an old French record
[01:38.00] Our history’s suddenly strangely checkered
[01:41.80] You hand me your jacket, the lining’s torn
[01:45.70] Swearing this fever is newly born
[01:49.40] But I know the cadence of an exit line
[01:53.30] Dressed up in vintage cabernet wine
[01:57.10] You kiss my collarbone, quick and polite
[02:00.60] Beneath the amber Edison string-bulb light
[Pre-Chorus]
[02:04.90] There’s a sudden bite in the evening air
[02:08.90] And you trace the rim of your crystal ware
[02:12.70] You look at the skyline, not at me
[02:16.40] Like a ship already out to sea
[Chorus]
[02:20.50] It’s copper on the terrace, gold turning to rust
[02:24.40] All of our promises ground into velvet dust
[02:28.40] Dance me to the edge of the balcony rail
[02:32.40] Before the warm trade winds begin to fail
[02:36.40] You’re holding my waist like a souvenir
[02:40.40] In the brightest hour of a dying year
[02:44.40] Yeah, it’s copper on the terrace tonight
[Bridge]
[02:52.50] Remember July on the fire escape?
[02:54.60] When every tomorrow had a reckless shape!
[02:56.50] Now you’re folding your secrets into your cuff
[02:58.30] As if wanting you once wasn't quite enough!
[03:00.10] Don't tell me the season is just a phase
[03:02.50] When I see the frost in your sideways gaze!
[Chorus]
[03:08.00] It’s copper on the terrace, gold turning to rust! (Turning to rust, baby!)
[03:12.00] All of our promises ground into velvet dust!
[03:16.00] Dance me to the edge of the balcony rail
[03:19.80] Before the warm trade winds begin to fail! (Don't let it fail now!)
[03:23.70] You’re holding my waist like a souvenir
[03:27.70] In the brightest hour of a dying year
[03:31.60] Yeah, it’s copper on the terrace tonight!
[Outro]
[03:41.00] Copper and rust on the avenue
[03:44.90] The air turns sharp between me and you
[03:48.80] Just a souvenir
[03:52.50] in the fading glow
